.TH CAT 1
.SH NAME
cat \- concatenate files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cat
[
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Cat
reads each
.I file
in sequence and writes it on the standard output.
Thus
.IP
.EX
cat file
.EE
.PP
prints a file and
.IP
.EX
cat file1 file2 >file3
.EE
.PP
concatenates the first two files and places the result
on the third.
.PP
If no
.I file
is given,
.I cat
reads from the standard input.
Data is copied in blocks of 4096 bytes.
A file that cannot be opened is reported on standard error
and the rest are still copied.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/cat/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR cp (1),
.IR read (1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty when every file was copied.
It is
.B "can't open"
when a file could not be opened, and
.B "read error"
when a read or a write failed.
.SH BUGS
.B cat a b >a
and
.B cat a b >b
destroy their input files before reading them.
